<section class="lf-article-section">
  <h2>Roofing leads for sale: pricing models explained</h2>

  <p>
    Roofing lead prices vary by service, location,
    qualification criteria, competition and
    lead-delivery model. A shared contact and a
    booked roofing inspection are not equivalent.
  </p>

  <h3>Shared roofing leads</h3>

  <p>
    Shared inquiries can be distributed to multiple
    roofing contractors. This may create direct
    competition for the same customer.
  </p>

  <h3>Exclusive roofing leads</h3>

  <p>
    Exclusive inquiries are generally intended
    for one contractor under the provider's terms.
    Verify the exclusivity policy, qualification
    process and invalid-lead replacement conditions.
  </p>

  <h3>Managed roofing lead generation</h3>

  <p>
    Managed services may include Google Ads,
    Facebook Ads, landing pages, lead qualification,
    CRM integration and follow-up automation.
    Contractors may pay advertising spend and
    management or implementation fees.
  </p>

  <p>
    LeadsFlo focuses on connected marketing and
    lead follow-through systems rather than
    reselling shared roofing lead lists.
  </p>

  <h3>How much do roofing leads cost?</h3>

  <p>
    There is no universal price. Compare cost
    per qualified inquiry, booked inspection
    and acquired customer using your own
    project values and sales performance.
  </p>

